#. PackedVector3Array.operator +
#: doc/classes/PackedVector3Array.xml
msgid "Returns a new [PackedVector3Array] with contents of [param right] added at the end of this array. For better performance, consider using [method append_array] instead."
msgstr "Új [PackedVector3Array] tömböt ad vissza, amely a tömb végéhez fűzve tartalmazza a [param right] elemeit. A jobb teljesítmény érdekében használd inkább a [method append_array] metódust."

#. PackedVector3Array.operator ==
#: doc/classes/PackedVector3Array.xml
msgid "Returns [code]true[/code] if contents of both arrays are the same, i.e. they have all equal [Vector3]s at the corresponding indices."
msgstr "[code]true[/code] értéket ad vissza, ha a tömbök tartalma megegyezik, vagyis azonos indexeken azonos [Vector3] értékeket tartalmaznak."

#. PackedVector3Array.operator []
#: doc/classes/PackedVector3Array.xml
msgid "Returns the [Vector3] at index [param index]. Negative indices can be used to access the elements starting from the end. Using index out of array's bounds will result in an error."
msgstr "Visszaadja a [param index] indexen lévő [Vector3] értéket. Negatív indexszel a tömb végétől érheted el az elemeket. Az érvényes indextartományon kívüli érték hibát okoz."

#. PackedVector4Array.brief
#: doc/classes/PackedVector4Array.xml
msgid "A packed array of [Vector4]s."
msgstr "[Vector4] értékek tömör tömbje."

#. PackedVector4Array.description
#: doc/classes/PackedVector4Array.xml
msgid "An array specifically designed to hold [Vector4]. Packs data tightly, so it saves memory for large array sizes.\n[b]Differences between packed arrays, typed arrays, and untyped arrays:[/b] Packed arrays are generally faster to iterate on and modify compared to a typed array of the same type (e.g. [PackedVector4Array] versus [code]Array[Vector4][/code]). Also, packed arrays consume less memory. As a downside, packed arrays are less flexible as they don't offer as many convenience methods such as [method Array.map]. Typed arrays are in turn faster to iterate on and modify than untyped arrays.\n[b]Note:[/b] Packed arrays are always passed by reference. To get a copy of an array that can be modified independently of the original array, use [method duplicate]. This is [i]not[/i] the case for built-in properties and methods. In these cases the returned packed array is a copy, and changing it will [i]not[/i] affect the original value. To update a built-in property of this type, modify the returned array and then assign it to the property again.\n[b]Note:[/b] In a boolean context, a packed array will evaluate to [code]false[/code] if it's empty. Otherwise, a packed array will always evaluate to [code]true[/code]."
